# Noble Hollow — the petrified tree

## Introduction

The Noble Hollow lies north of Atomer along a river that flows toward the great lake. Far from familiar roads, the earth hardens into waves of pale stone and the living trees become twisted statues. Their trunks preserve gaping holes and knots like faces caught mid-cry. Many insects move across these dead forms, lending a suggestion of life to a place that has little of it. A particularly great tree dominates the clearing, its old limbs raised like arms over ground that local guild members know as powerful and ill-favored.[^setting]

## The midnight ceremony

A guild researcher called Marek brings a kidnapped high elf to the clearing. Faelan lies unconscious atop a circular, gear-edged stone while green flames circle around him, and two robed followers attend their master. A silver-ranked warlock stands nearby, and another bronze adventurer named Norman is bound on the ground. The researcher believes a ritual involving devotion, sacrifice and the ancient stone can call a beast from the lake, though its larger consequence remains a prediction rather than an accomplished event. His choice of this hollow relies upon the place's unsettling character and old power.[^rite]

The Darkest Delvers arrive with Broadside and Boonefellow. Broadside takes hold of Solburn rather than attacking him, while the Delvers try to interrupt the rite before midnight. Their struggle ends when Evelyn brings the researcher down without killing him. The stone breaks beneath Faelan, and the green flames go out. Before anyone can claim safety, the ground buckles, the old roots crack and most of the clearing falls into an immense underground cavity. Water rushes over the edge of the broken ground and into the darkness.[^break]

## The cavern beneath

A massive stalagmite turns out to be a great roper, an apparently stony predator whose jaws and tendrils are far larger than the creatures the guild has recently found near the city. Piercers climb its cavern walls, and smaller ones emerge from a crevice in its lower body. The Delvers and their allies fight it among falling water, loose rock and victims of the collapse. Evelyn finally drives a javelin into its breeding aperture, and the beast's desperate movements end in its death. Faelan and Norman are pulled from danger and healed alive, but a fallen cultist is swallowed before the battle ends.[^roper]

## Current status

The Noble Hollow's **surface clearing has collapsed** into a water-filled underground cavern; the **great roper is dead**. **Marek's ritual is interrupted**, its **geared sacrificial stone shattered**, and the two kidnapped guild members rescued alive. Many **piercers survive and scatter**, and no completed geological survey, rebuilding, sealing or cleansing of this place is shown. The exact relation between the shattered disk, the smaller geared fragment recovered beneath the lake and the still-unknown power of the Dawnless Dunes remains open.[^status]

[^setting]: [Delvers S1E12](../../episodes/S1E12.md), ~01:19–01:35. Site described via played forest and map; coordinates, ownership and past history unknown. Researcher/guild describe place as “unhallowed,” their classification not an objective history.
[^rite]: [S1E12](../../episodes/S1E12.md), ~01:08–01:16 and ~01:33–01:59. Cheet gives ritual requirements; observed green flames/high elf/disc and two attendants. “Beast of the lake” is projected summon, not seen arrive.
[^break]: [S1E12](../../episodes/S1E12.md), ~01:59–02:12. Nonlethal defeat breaks ritual; disk's collapse triggers local destruction. Mechanism causation likely in GM account, but exact underworld process unexplained.
[^roper]: [S1E12](../../episodes/S1E12.md), ~02:12–02:49. GM identifies roper name, piercers emerge as offspring, one cultist swallowed; Faelan and Norman healed alive by Evelyn.
[^status]: [S1E12](../../episodes/S1E12.md), ~02:49 onward, immediate event then postscene debrief; no explicit follow-up journey to hollow shown. Season-one/first-arc end, ASR provisional.
